/**
 * Still Waters (docs/storychains.html, Chain B): twenty missions that start with a crate of fish for the
 * aquarium and end with the fleet on the quay of a dry dock at dawn as a submarine floats out of it.
 *
 * Skipper Maren Holt nets a fish with no eyes and a tile that hums. Dr Teodor Lind can't name either. Old
 * Fen the lighthouse keeper has seen lights under the water for forty years, in sevens. CPO Rook's
 * coastguard, Greywater Salvage stealing tiles, Starlight Pictures and its free-diver Lio Brandt, a Navy
 * carrier off the harbour and Commander Yusra Adeyemi. The lamp flashes sevens; the sea answers in eights.
 * "It's a door." By the nineteenth mission Adeyemi says it plainly: the Navy needs haulage on the bottom
 * of the ocean. The twenty-first mission, the dive itself, is not in the game.
 */
